{
  "id": "EUVD-2025-35712",
  "enisaUuid": "7fbea00a-7dac-3074-9702-eda8fed6dce3",
  "description": "A container privilege escalation flaw was found in certain Container-native Virtualization images. This issue stems from the /etc/passwd file being created with group-writable permissions during build time. In certain conditions, an attacker who can execute commands within an affected container, even as a non-root user, can leverage their membership in the root group to modify the /etc/passwd file. This could allow the attacker to add a new user with any arbitrary UID, including UID 0, leading to full root privileges within the container.",
  "datePublished": "Oct 23, 2025, 8:10:31 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Aug 6, 2026, 10:50:31 AM",
